{"id":"hep-th/9601134","updated":"2023-12-13T13:25:20.274102+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/hep-th/9601134?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/hep-th/9601134?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/hep-th/9601134?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/hep-th/9601134?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/hep-th/9601134?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/arxiv/hep-th/9601134?format=cv"},"metadata":{"publication_info":[{"year":1996,"page_end":"2534","page_start":"2519","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volume":"54"}],"report_numbers":[{"value":"PSU-TH-167"}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":172,"citation_count":225,"core":true,"dois":[{"value":"10.1103/PhysRevD.54.2519"}],"titles":[{"title":"Thermal properties of an inflationary universe"},{"title":"Thermal Properties of an Inflationary Universe","source":"arXiv"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","authors":[{"uuid":"2f3f78cf-96f1-4e5b-9f94-58b25ec37548","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1016688"},"full_name":"Berera, Arjun","affiliations":[{"value":"Penn State U.","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903125"}}],"signature_block":"BARARa"}],"curated":true,"texkeys":["Berera:1996nv"],"citeable":true,"keywords":[{"value":"05.40.+j","schema":"PACS"},{"value":"98.80.Cq","schema":"PACS"},{"value":"inflation","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"density: fluctuation","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"temperature: fluctuation","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"field theory: inflaton","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"Langevin equation","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"statistical mechanics","schema":"INSPIRE"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"An energetic justification of a thermal component during inflation is given. The thermal component can act as a heat reservoir which induces thermal fluctuations on the inflaton field system. We showed previously that such thermal fluctuations could dominate quantum fluctuations in producing the initial seeds of density perturbations. A Langevin-like rate equation is derived from quantum field theory which describes the production of fluctuations in the inflaton field when acted upon by a simple modeled heat reservoir. In a certain limit this equation is shown to reduce to the standard Langevin equation, which we used to construct \"Warm Inflation\" scenarios in previous work. A particle physics interpretation of our system-reservoir model is offered."}],"references":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/154280"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"347","page_start":"347","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volume":"23"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/182708"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"1110","page_start":"1110","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett.","journal_volume":"49"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/13328"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"679","page_start":"679","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volume":"28"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/196244"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"177","page_start":"177","journal_title":"Phys.Lett.B","journal_volume":"129"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/192777"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"2172","page_start":"2172","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volume":"29"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/216115"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"273","page_start":"273","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D","journal_volume":"31"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/333970"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"L1","page_start":"L1","jour